<title>AUSTRALIA: CRICKET-SHEFFIELD SHIELD SCORES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-SHEFFIELD SHIELD SCORES.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-01-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scores in four-day Sheffield Shield cricket matches on Saturday:</p>
<p>In Sydney (third day): New South Wales 126 and 337 (Rodney Davison 99); Western Australia 244 (Brad Hogg 59, Brad McNamara five for 75) and 166 for one (Mike Hussey 58 not out).</p>
<p>In Melbourne (third day): Tasmania 359 for seven declared (Daniel Marsh 97) and 182 for three; Victoria 284 for nine declared.</p>
<p>In Adelaide (second day): South Australia 527 for six declared (Darren Lehmann 255); Queensland 143 for six.</p>
